cess to C4 and E2. By playing F5, you maintain a compact shape and force the opponent into a more difficult position.\n\nReason: F5 is the best move because it strengthens center control without giving the opponent easy tactical responses. Unlike F4 and F2, which open up the C4 square for the opponent (allowing them to flip central pieces), F5 keeps the opponent restricted. It is a "quiet" move that preserves mobility.\n\nAnswer: (F, 5)'}
